Article 14
Special protection for children is provided to;
(1)
a. Children in emergency situations;
b. Children in conflict with the law;
c. Children from minority and isolated groups;
d. Children who are exploited economically and/or sexually;
e. Children who are victims of narcotics abuse, alcohol, psychotropics, and other addictive substances;
f. Children who are victims of pornography;
g. Children with HIV/AIDS;
h. Children who are victims of kidnapping, sale, and/or trafficking;
i. Children who are victims of physical and/or psychological violence;
j. Children who are victims of sexual crimes;
k. Children who are victims of terrorist networks;
l. Children with Disabilities;
m. Children who are victims of maltreatment and neglect;
n. Children with deviant social behavior; and
o. Children who are victims of stigmatization from labeling related to the condition of their Parents.
(2) Regional governments in implementing the handling referred to in paragraph (1) shall be in accordance with the provisions of the Laws and Regulations.

CHAPTER II
PRINCIPLES AND OBJECTIVES
Article 2
The Protection of Women and Children from Acts of Violence, is implemented based on the principles of:
a. respect and fulfillment of the rights of Victims of Acts of Violence;
b. justice and gender equality;
c. non-discrimination;
d. the best interests of Victims of acts of violence; and
e. The principle of the right to life, survival and development,

Article 3
The objectives of the protection of women and children from acts of violence are to:
a. prevent violence against women and children including trafficking in persons;
b. eliminate all forms of violence and exploitation against women and children;
c. protect and provide a sense of security for women and children; d. provide services and Empowerment to women and children victims of violence, reporters and witnesses; e. facilitate and conduct mediation of domestic disputes to realize the integrity of a harmonious and prosperous household; and
f. Facilitate the restoration of the rights, dignity and personal value of victims.

Article 5
The Regional Government is responsible for efforts to protect women from acts of violence that occur in public or private life in the form of:
a. physical violence;
b. sexual violence;
c. economic violence;
d. social violence;
e. psychological violence;
f. domestic neglect;
g. coercion or deprivation of freedom; and
h. threats of certain actions.

Article 16
(1) The Regional Government in conducting cooperation and coordination regarding the Protection of Women and Children from acts of violence, shall establish a Forum for the Care of Women and Children from Acts of Violence (FP2ATK);
(2) The membership of FP2ATK consists of elements:
a. regional government;
b. vertical agencies;
c. educational institutions;
d. health institutions;
e. social institutions;
f. labor institutions; and
g. community organizations that care about the protection of women and children from acts of violence.
(3) The Organizational Structure of FP2ATK as referred to in paragraph (2) consists of:
a. policy formulation working group;
b. socialization working group;
b. service working group; and
c. data, information, monitoring and evaluation working group.
(4) The establishment and term of office of FP2ATK members as referred to in paragraph (1), shall be stipulated by Regent's Decree.

Article 7
(1) Regional Government conducts prevention as referred to in article 6 letter a by means of: a. socializing laws and regulations- b. providing counseling/guidance; c. providing education on the dangers of domestic violence; d. conducting seminars/workshops or the like; e. establishing work networks in efforts to prevent violence; f. conducting coordination, integration, synchronization of violence prevention based on partnership patterns; g. establishing a violence prevention system, mapping of locations or areas prone to violence; and h. increasing public awareness in behaving in accordance with religious norms and customs (2) In addition to the Regional Government, prevention as referred to in paragraph (1) must be implemented by:
a. Religious institutions;
b. family and/or closest relatives;
c. customary leaders;
d. customary institutions;
e. community;
f. educational institutions;
g. health institutions;
h. social community institutions; and i. business sector and other institutions.

Article 13
(1) The provisions regarding prevention and services for acts of violence protection of women as referred to in Article 7 through Article 12 shall apply mutatis mutandis to the protection of children from acts of violence;
(2) In addition to carrying out prevention as referred to in paragraph (1), also by means of increasing family capacity in child protection and child care skills.

Pasal 8
(1) Pemerintah Daerah berkewajiban menyusun program atau kegiatan Pencegahan sebagaimana dimaksud dalam Pasal 7 ayat (1) dalam Rencana Keija dan Rencana Strategis Daerah;
(2) Program atau kegiatan sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (1) untuk mendukung terwujudnya Rencana Pembangunan Jangka Panjang Daerah dan Rencana Pembangunan Jangka Menengah Daerah.

Article 8
(1) Regional Governments are obligated to formulate Prevention programs or activities as referred to in Article 7 paragraph (1) in the Regional Work Plan and Regional Strategic Plan;
(2) Programs or activities as referred to in paragraph (1) are to support the realization of the Regional Long-Term Development Plan and Regional Medium-Term Development Plan.

Article 12
(1) The protection of children who are victims of acts of violence as referred to in article 5 letter a shall be the responsibility of the Regional Government. (2) The protection of child victims of acts of violence as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be implemented by means of: a. formulating policies for prevention, reduction of vulnerable risks, handling of victims and child data and information systems; b. providing maintenance, care, and social rehabilitation for neglected children, both within institutions and outside institutions;
c. providing shelters, maintenance and care for neglected children; and d. providing special protection to children.

